{
  "stem": "advanced_shipping_2023_W51_ADVANCED-MARKET-REPORT-WEEK-51",
  "source_file": "advanced_shipping_2023_W51_ADVANCED-MARKET-REPORT-WEEK-51.pdf",
  "issue_date": "2023-12-22",
  "report_week": "51",
  "report_period": "Week 51 (15th Dec to 22nd Dec 2023)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "The Kamsarmax \"Ultra Tiger\" 83/2009 Sanoyas, Japan (SS/DD 05/2026, BWTS fitted) was committed to Indian buyers for USD 16,5 mill. Remind you that the one-year-younger sister vessel \"IC Harvest\" 83/2010 Sanoyas, Japan (SS/DD 02/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold a couple of weeks ago at USD 17 mill. Furthermore, Nisshin Shipping sold their \"Presinge Trader\" 81/2016 Jiangsu, China (SS 12/2026, DD 02/2025, BWTS fitted) to clients of W Marine for high USD 25 mill. Note that the one-year-older Scrubber fitted \"Pedhoulas Cherry\" 82/2015 Jiangsu, China (SS/DD 07/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) was sold earlier this month at USD 26,6 mill. On the Ultramax sector, the \"Xing Xi Hai\" 60/2017 Mitsui, Japan (SS 01/2027, DD 01/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed to Scandinavian interests at USD 29 mill, while the one-year-older sister vessel \"Xing Shou Hai\" 60/2016 Mitsui, Japan (SS 10/2026, DD 10/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold to Greek interests at USD 28 mill. For reference, the \"Santa Francesca\" 61/2016 Shin Kasado, Japan (SS 01/2026, DD 01/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold back in October at USD 26,8 mill. The Supramax \"Supra Oniki\" 57/2010 Qingshan, China (SS/DD 07/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed to undisclosed buyers at excess USD 11 mill. Remind you that back in September, the two-years-younger sister vessel \"Supra Thessal\" 57/2012 Qingshan, China (SS/DD 01/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 11,5 mill. Following the sale of the Handysize \"Clipper Como\" 37/2010 Huatai, China (SS/DD 10/2025, BWTS fitted, Ice Class 1C) earlier this month at USD 10,9 mill, Clipper Bulk have now committed the \"Clipper Copenhagen\" 37/2010 Jiangsu, China (SS 06/2025, DD 01/2026, BWTS fitted, Ice Class 1C) for low USD 11 mill.",
    "tankers": "Great Eastern Shipping have committed their MR2 \"Jag Prabha\" 48/2004 Iwagi, Japan (SS 09/2027, DD 09/2025, BWTS fitted) to undisclosed buyers for region USD 15 mill. Remind you that back in August, the \"Scarlet Ibis\" 46/2004 Iwagi, Japan (SS/DD 01/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold at the same levels. The MR1 \"Blue Trader\" 37/2005 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS/DD 03/2025, BWTS fitted, Ice Class 1B) was sold to Turkish buyers Besiktas for region USD 17,6 mill. For comparison, the one-year-younger \"Baltic Mariner I\" 37/2006 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 10/2026, DD 12/2024, BWTS fitted, Ice Class 1B) was sold in October at USD 18,5 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of mid-high usd 13,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 13,000/15,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were fixed around usd 13,000/16,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into India were reported at the level of usd 14,000/15,000 pd. Australian trips into South Africa were fixed around usd 12,000/14,000 pd. South East Asian trips via South America into China were fixed around usd 15,000/19,000 pd. Indian trips via South America into China were reported at the level of usd 14,000/17,000 pd. West African trips via South America into Continent were fixed around usd 21,000/23,000 pd. Continental trips via US East Coast and India into South Africa were reported at the level of usd 20,000/22,000 pd. Inter-Continental trips via Baltic were fixed around usd 22,000/24,000 pd. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed at the level of usd 11,500 pd for 4/6 months employment basis delivery China. Also, a Kamsarmax was fixed on period at the usd 16,000 pd basis delivery China for 1 year employment.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 10,000/12,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were fixed around usd 7,000/9,000 pd. Trips from China via Vancouver into South Africa were reported at the level of usd 7,000 for first 65 days usd 12,500 balance. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "A number of Australian trips into South East Asia were fixed around usd 8,000/9,000 pd. Continental trips into US Gulf were reported at the level of usd 18,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 23,000/25,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
